{"publishers": ["The Penguin Press"], "number_of_pages": 256, "table_of_contents": [{"level": 0, "label": "", "title": "Introduction: A guide for the perplexed", "pagenum": ""}, {"level": 0, "label": "1", "title": "The way we live now", "pagenum": ""}, {"level": 0, "label": "2", "title": "The world we have lost", "pagenum": ""}, {"level": 0, "label": "3", "title": "The unbearable lightness of politics", "pagenum": ""}, {"level": 0, "label": "4", "title": "Goodbye to all that?", "pagenum": ""}, {"level": 0, "label": "5", "title": "What is to be done?", "pagenum": ""}, {"level": 0, "label": "6", "title": "The shape of things to come", "pagenum": ""}, {"level": 0, "label": "", "title": "Conclusion: What is living and what is dead in social democracy.", "pagenum": ""}], "covers": [6953967], "physical_format": "Hardcover", "lc_classifications": ["D860 .J83 2010", "D860.J83 2010"], "key": "/books/OL24523595M", "authors": [{"key": "/authors/OL226798A"}], "ocaid": "illfareslandtrea00judt", "publish_places": ["USA"], "isbn_13": ["9781594202766"], "classifications": {}, "source_records": ["marc:marc_loc_updates/v38.i33.records.utf8:30193634:1352", "ia:illfareslandtrea00judt", "marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run04.mrc:64884005:4324", "marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part37.utf8:118543098:1827", "ia:illfaresland0000judt", "bwb:9781594202766", "marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-016.mrc:122490179:2418", "marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.12.20150123.full.mrc:320192368:1947", "marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_029.bib.mrc:94892028:3077"], "subtitle": "A Treatise On Our Present Discontents", "title": "Ill Fares The Land", "lccn": ["2010006963"], "notes": "Includes bibliographical references.", "identifiers": {}, "languages": [{"key": "/languages/eng"}], "dewey_decimal_class": ["909.83/1"], "local_id": ["urn:sfpl:31223092775775", "urn:sfpl:31223092664979", "urn:sfpl:31223092664896", "urn:sfpl:31223092664995", "urn:sfpl:31223092775858", "urn:sfpl:31223092665018", "urn:sfpl:31223092777623", "urn:sfpl:31223092777615", "urn:sfpl:31223092664888"], "publish_date": "18 March 2010", "publish_country": "nyu", "copyright_date": "2010", "oclc_numbers": ["526057518"], "works": [{"key": "/works/OL15571084W"}], "type": {"key": "/type/edition"}, "physical_dimensions": "8.26 x 5.51 x  inches", "description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "In \"Ill Fares The Land,\" Tony Judt, one of our leading historians and thinkers, reveals how we have arrived at our present dangerously confused moment and offers the language we need to address our common needs, rejecting the nihilistic individualism of the far right and the debunked socialism of the past. To find a way forward, Judt argues that we must look to our not so distant past and to social democracy in action: to re-enshrining fairness over mere efficiency."}, "latest_revision": 15, "revision": 15, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2010-12-09T16:30:29.288247"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2026-01-30T19:10:42.577283"}}